# Breaks R-2: only what a module marks `pub` is reachable from outside it, and
# `greeting` in `dep/greeter` carries no `pub`. Qualifying the call does not get
# around that. It has to be genuinely unreachable rather than merely absent
# from a `using`, because a `.iyimod` carries a module's exports and nothing
# else, so if another module could call an unmarked name that artifact would
# not be enough to compile against.
module diagnostics/r2_not_exported

import dep/greeter

puts Dep::Greeter.greeting
